===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[violent]] [[collision]] or [[compression]]; a [[crash]]; [[destruction]]; [[ruin]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1921|author= Alexis Thomson; Alexander Miles|title=Manual of Surgery|passage=The more highly the injured part is endowed with sensory nerves the more marked is the shock; a '''crush''' of the hand, for example, is attended with a more intense degree of shock than a correspondingly severe '''crush''' of the foot}}
# [[violent|Violent]] [[pressure]], as of a [[move|moving]] [[crowd]].
# A [[violent]] [[crowding]].
# A [[crowd]] that [[produce]]s [[uncomfortable]] [[pressure]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''crush''' at a reception}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A group or gang.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=302|passage=Then there was another set who called themselves the "Ragged Thirteen"; and the account says "they looked it." And, like most diggers, this "'''crush'''," to quote my authority, could handle the cards a bit.}}
# A [[crowd control]] [[barrier]].
# A [[drink]] made by [[squeeze|squeezing]] the [[juice]] out of [[fruit]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1958|year_published=1972|author=w:Anthony Burgess|title=The Enemy in the Blanket|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=292|passage="Look," said Crabbe, warm orange '''crush''' in his hand.}}
# {{senseid|en|infatuation}}{{lb|en|informal}} An [[infatuation]] with somebody one is not [[date|dating]].
#: {{ux|en|I've had a huge '''crush''' on her since we met many years ago.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2019|author=Emma Lea|title=A Royal Enticement
|passage=And I needed to get my schoolgirl '''crush''' under control. There was no way Brín felt anything anywhere near what I felt for him. He saw me as a friend.}}
## {{lb|en|informal|by extension}} The human object of such infatuation or [[affection]].
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=[[w: Chris Wallace (journalist)|Chris Wallace]]|title=Character: Profiles in Presidential Courage
|passage=It had taken nine years from the evening that {{w|Harry Truman|Truman}} first showed up with a pie plate at her mother's door, but his dogged perseverance eventually won him the hand of his boyhood Sunday school '''crush'''.}}
# A [[standing stock]] or [[cage]] with [[movable]] [[side]]s used to [[restrain]] [[livestock]] for [[safe]] [[handling]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[party]] or [[festive]] [[function]].
#* {{RQ:Wilde Dorian Gray|text=Two months ago I went to a '''crush''' at Lady Brandon's.|1}}
# {{lb|en|Australia}} The process of [[#Verb|crush]]ing [[cane]] to [[remove]] the [[raw]] [[sugar]], or the [[season]] when this process takes place.
# {{lb|en|television|uncountable}} The situation where certain [[color]]s are so [[similar]] as to be [[hard]] to [[distinguish]], either as a [[deliberate]] [[effect]] or as a [[limitation]] of a [[display]].
#: {{ux|en|black '''crush'''; white '''crush'''}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|sexuality}} A [[paraphilia]] involving [[arousal]] from [[see]]ing things [[destroy]]ed by [[#Verb|crush]]ing.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Katharine Gates|title=Deviant Desires: Incredibly Strange Sex|page=137
|passage=Just as they say that marijuana leads to harder drugs, Gallegly is claiming that '''crush''' is a "gateway fetish"—a term I've never heard before. He claims that if someone starts with bugs they'll end up escalating to human babies in no time.}}

