===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[press]] [[between]] two [[hard]] [[object]]s; to [[squeeze]] so as to [[alter]] the [[natural]] [[shape]] or [[integrity]], or to [[force]] together into a [[mass]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''crush''' grapes}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1769|author=Benjamin Blayney|title=King James Bible|section=Leviticus 22:24
|passage=Ye shall not offer unto the {{smallcaps|Lord}} that which is bruised, or '''crushed''', or broken, or cut}}
# To [[reduce]] to [[fine]] [[particle]]s by [[pound]]ing or [[grind]]ing.
#: {{syn|en|comminute}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''crush''' quartz}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Tarzan of the Apes|1|passage=With a wild scream he was upon her, tearing a great piece from her side with his mighty teeth, and striking her viciously upon her head and shoulders with a broken tree limb until her skull was '''crushed''' to a jelly.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[overwhelm]] by [[pressure]] or [[weight]].
#: {{ux|en|After the corruption scandal, the opposition '''crushed''' the ruling party in the elections}}
#* {{quote-av
|en
|date=September 1, 1950
|author=w:Harry S. Truman
|title=MP72-73 Korea and World Peace: President Truman Reports to the People
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fMDAbVD9yx0
|publisher=w:Harry S. Truman Presidential Library and Museum
|id=National Archives Identifier: [https://catalog.archives.gov/id/595162 595162]
|time=2:02
|text=We believe the invasion has reached its peak. The task remaining is to '''crush''' it. Our men are confident, the United Nations command is confident, that it will be '''crushed'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=November 11, 2011
|author=Rory Houston
|title=Estonia 0-4 Republic of Ireland
|work=RTE Sport
|url=http://www.rte.ie/sport/soccer/2011/1111/estonia_ireland_report.html
|page=
|passage=A stunning performance from the Republic of Ireland all but sealed progress to Euro 2012 as they '''crushed''' nine-man Estonia 4-0 in the first leg of the qualifying play-off tie in A Le Coq Arena in Tallinn.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|colloquial}} To do [[impressively]] well at ([[sports]] [[event]]s; [[performance]]s; [[interview]]s; etc.).
#: {{ux|en|They had a gig recently at Madison Square—totally '''crushed''' it!}}
# To [[oppress]] or [[grievously]] [[burden]].
# {{senseid|en|subdue}} To [[overcome]] completely; to [[subdue]] totally.
#: {{ux|en|The sultan's black guard '''crushed''' every resistance bloodily.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1814|author=Sir Walter Scott|title=Waverley|passage=the prospect of the Duke's speedily overtaking and '''crushing''' the rebels}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be or become [[broken down]] or in, or [[press]]ed into a smaller [[volume]] or [[area]], by external [[weight]] or [[force]].
#: {{ux|en|an eggshell '''crushes''' easily}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive}} To feel [[infatuation]] or [[unrequited]] [[love]].
#: {{ux|en|She's '''crushing''' on him.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Aaron’s Party (Come Get It)|year=2000|artist=w:Aaron Carter|passage=Then walked in / The girl I'm '''crushin{{'}}''' / And the kid spilled juice / On my Mom's new cushion}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011 |title=Love Is Blind |author=May'lon Miranda  |page=58 |ISBN=1467070173|passage=... I could just let loose and be myself  no holding back you know we just where to young kids in love, lust, '''crushing''' whatever you wanted to call it but we where living it up having fun when we where together the rest of the world didn't exist ...}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=Diary of a Crush: Kiss and Make Up|author=Sarra Manning  |page= |ISBN=1405525797|passage=And the one subject that I get an A plus in every time, is the ancient art of '''crushing'''. I '''crush''', therefore I am. I've decided to share the benefit of my wisdom and after months of hopelessly lusting after Dylan, I've REALISED that there are twelve degrees of '''crushing''' from the slightly embarrassing things most girls will do to catch the eye of the heir to their heart, to the verging on ridiculous stunts you pull when you're in the grip of  a passion that renders you powerless.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013 |title=Zen Confidential: Confessions of a Wayward Monk |author=Shozan Jack Haubner |page= 130|ISBN=1611800331|passage="I respect your wiring," he explained, "but I'm '''crushing''' on you. And when I '''crush''', I '''crush''' hard." He thought it would be better if we stopped seeing each other for a while. }}
# {{lb|en|film|television}} To give a [[compress]]ed or [[foreshorten]]ed [[appearance]] to.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Michel Chion|title=The Films of Jacques Tati|page=78
|passage=He frames his subject in distant close-ups (we feel the distance, due mostly to the '''crushed''' perspective brought about by the telephoto lens).}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Birgit Bräuchler; John Postill|title=Theorising Media and Practice|page=319
|passage=They realise that trajectories, space expansion and '''crushing''' are different with different lenses, whether wide angle or telephoto, and that actors' eyelines will be altered.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|television}} To make certain [[color]]s so [[similar]] as to be [[hard]] to [[distinguish]], either as a [[deliberate]] [[effect]] or as a [[limitation]] of a [[display]].
#: {{ux|en|My old TV set '''crushes''' the blacks when the brightness is lowered.}}

